Z||000000||LAMBO||02-21-2001||10:59 AM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2.5supercharger.jpg">  <BR>If I am not mistaken, Jeep uses the same 2.5l duke motor that is in our beloved Fieros. The company claims hp ratings in the 185 range on a stock motor. Just need to ditch the dogbone (fabricate an upper brace somewhere else), change to serpentine pullies and viola, you're off to the races. With some minor engine mods, better exhaust, a little flow work on the heads, different cam, I think 200hp+ would be achievable. I wouldn't want to put this on a high mile motor though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Todd<BR>go here <A HREF="http://www.rimmersuperchargers.com/jeep.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rimmersuperchargers.com/jeep.html</A>  <p>[This message has been edited by LAMBO (edited 02-21-2001).]||||reg||14
